# Version control
.git
.gitignore

# Dependencies (rebuilt in container — root only; workspace node_modules needed by COPY)
/node_modules
.venv
__pycache__
*.pyc
*.pyo

# Data files (bulk scraped corpora — the corpus itself lives in Postgres + ES).
# Exclude the CONTENTS of data/ rather than the directory itself: a bare
# `data/` directory-exclusion is re-includable on current BuildKit, but the
# contents form (`data/*`) is the portable spelling that keeps the `!`
# re-inclusions below working across builder versions.
#
# The REGISTRY files are re-included on purpose: they are code-adjacent metadata,
# not corpus. Every in-pod registry operation reads them — `LawRegistry`
# (apps/scraper/utils/law_registry.py) defaults to data/law_registry.json, the
# `dataops.ingest_law` Celery task resolves law ids through it, and
# apps/scraper/dataops/coverage_dashboard.py reads both. Without them in the image
# these all die with FileNotFoundError (bit us live on the 2026-08-27 LFPDPPP
# Reglamento ingest, worked around by hand-copying into the pod).
#
# universe_registry.json is re-included for the same class of reason: it is the
# source of the coverage universe counts served by /api/v1/coverage/ and
# /api/v1/stats/. Excluding it made the public /cobertura page fall back to
# hardcoded literals (e.g. "state legislation 12,468 / 100%") that were never
# measured against the database. It is tracked in git for the same reason (see
# the `!` rule in .gitignore). Nothing else under data/ ships.
data/*
!data/law_registry.json
!data/discovered_reglamentos.json
!data/universe_registry.json
db.sqlite3

# Documentation
docs/
*.md
!README.md

